ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
Alternative vertices considered: runners, cap centers, components, owners,
primary n-cells, upper/lower half-caps, and proof obligations.
Chosen vertices are proof certificates.  The quotient preserves whether
owner bisection forces mass into one-sided cap capacity.  It destroys
exact phase order inside a cell; any mixed fiber must be lifted by
endpoint owner, side, and residue labels.
